[B]About[/B]

Unofficial CyanogenMod 10 (Android 4.1.2 Jelly Bean) port for the LG L5 II E450g, codename [B]vee5ss[/B], SoC MediaTek MT6575.

This build uses the stock prebuilt kernel and a MediaTek-format boot image generated with [B]mtkbootimg[/B]. The OTA zip updates [B]/system only[/B] — you must flash [B]boot.img separately[/B] via dd (see install instructions).

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: LG L5 II / LG-E450g
[*]Codename: vee5ss
[*]SoC: MediaTek MT6575, ARMv7-A Cortex-A9, 1 GHz
[*]RAM: 512 MB
[*]Display: 4.0" 480×800 hdpi, SLCD
[*]Storage: 4 GB internal / external microSD
[*]Android: 4.1.2 Jelly Bean (JZO54K)
[/LIST]

[B]Current status — Build 2 (2026-06-30)[/B]

Functional beta. Core system, GPU, radio stack, IMEI, SIM PIN unlock, and calls are all confirmed working.

[B]Working / verified[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Boots to Android (sys.boot_completed=1)
[*]Display + touchscreen
[*]Hardware acceleration — PowerVR SGX531 binary blobs
[*]SurfaceFlinger, Launcher, Settings, core apps
[*]WiFi (connected, verified)
[*]Bluetooth stack running
[*]External microSD at /storage/sdcard1
[*]Internal storage (FUSE/datamedia) at /storage/sdcard0
[*]Settings > Storage
[*]LCD brightness control
[*]Notification LED — custom lights HAL, no stuck-on bug
[*]Sensors: accelerometer, magnetometer, orientation, proximity
[*]IMEI confirmed — stock lgpserver reads from /dev/misc2
[*]Baseband version visible (MAUI.11AMD.TC1.V5.SP.V0.P16)
[*]RIL connected: gsm.version.ril-impl = mtk gemini ril 1.0
[*]Modem boots on first attempt (~7 s, no 23 s WDT timeout/reset)
[*]zRAM ~120 MB swap active (ro.zram.default=25, managed by CM10 compcache)
[*]Offline charging
[*]ADB root (ro.secure=0, development build)
[*]SIM PIN unlock — keyguard shows PIN dialog on boot; PIN accepted; SIM transitions to READY
[*]Outgoing calls — connected and audible; earpiece and microphone working
[*]Proximity sensor — screen turns off during calls as expected
[/LIST]

[B]Not tested / pending[/B]
[LIST]
[*]SMS
[*]Mobile data
[*]Camera — HAL in place, not tested
[*]GPS — agpsd daemon included, not tested
[*]FM Radio — not tested
[/LIST]

[B]Known bugs[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]MediaScanner SIGSEGV[/B] — if your microSD has folders with Latin-1 encoded characters in the name (e.g. a folder originally named "Imágenes" that shows as "ImM-agenes" on Linux), MediaScanner aborts on invalid UTF-8. Remove the offending folder from your SD via a PC before inserting.
[*][B]Audio NVRAM calibration missing[/B] — /data/nvram/APCFG/APRDEB/ is empty after clean flash. Audio output works, but EQ/compensation filter is unavailable. Workaround: copy calibration data from a TWRP backup of the stock ROM.
[*][B]WMT stp_dump NULL[/B] — harmless logcat noise at boot during Combo chip WMT init; no functional impact.
[*][B]Screen stays off after call ends[/B] — PhoneApp may not release the proximity wakelock if the call ends while the proximity sensor is active (e.g. phone held to ear). Screen appears dead but system is alive. Workaround: reboot. Does not affect calls in progress.
[/LIST]

[B]Important notes[/B]
[LIST]
[*]This ROM is for [B]LG-E450g / vee5ss ONLY[/B]. Do not flash on any other L5 II variant.
[*]TWRP recovery required — standard CWM does not support the MTK EMMC partition layout on this device.
[*][B]The OTA zip updates /system only.[/B] You must flash boot.img separately via dd (see Install instructions).
[*]Make a full Nandroid backup before flashing.
[*]Back up your NVRAM partition to protect your IMEI and calibration data before testing any MTK ROM.
[*]GApps: use a Jelly Bean compatible package. CM10 GApps from the era are recommended.
[/LIST]

[B]Requirements[/B]
[LIST]
[*]LG-E450g (vee5ss) — tested hardware only
[*]TWRP recovery (MTK-compatible build for this device)
[*]At least 30% battery charge
[*]Full Nandroid backup (strongly recommended)
[/LIST]

[B]Install — clean flash[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Copy the ROM zip AND boot.img to your SD card.
[*]Boot into TWRP recovery.
[*]Make a full Nandroid backup.
[*]Wipe: Data / Factory Reset, Cache, Dalvik Cache.
[*]Flash the ROM zip (this updates /system only).
[*]Optional: flash a Jelly Bean compatible GApps package.
[*]Flash boot.img from the TWRP shell:
[CODE]dd if=/sdcard/boot.img of=/dev/bootimg bs=4096[/CODE]
[*]Reboot System.
[/LIST]

[B]Install — dirty flash / update from older build[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Boot into TWRP.
[*]Make a backup.
[*]Flash the new ROM zip.
[*]Flash the new boot.img from the TWRP shell:
[CODE]dd if=/sdcard/boot.img of=/dev/bootimg bs=4096[/CODE]
[*]Wipe Cache and Dalvik Cache.
[*]Reboot System.
[/LIST]

[B]Troubleshooting[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Kernel panic / VFS: Unable to mount root fs on unknown-block(1,0)[/B] — boot.img was not flashed or the flash failed. Reboot to TWRP and run:
[CODE]dd if=/sdcard/boot.img of=/dev/bootimg bs=4096[/CODE]
[*][B]Bootloop after first flash[/B] — wipe Dalvik cache and cache in TWRP, then reboot.
[*][B]No internal storage / Settings > Storage crash[/B] — should not occur; the storage_list.xml overlay is included in this build.
[*][B]MediaScanner crash (SIGSEGV in logcat)[/B] — remove any folder with non-ASCII Latin-1 characters from your microSD before first boot.
[*][B]No signal after SIM insert[/B] — reboot the device after inserting the SIM; hot-swap is not supported on MT6575.
[/LIST]

