[B]Changelog[/B]

[B]2026-06-29 — Build 2[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]IMEI fix[/B] — replaced hand-written lgpservicestub (returned zeros for Binder transaction 111) with stock lgpserver binary reading IMEI directly from /dev/misc2. IMEI confirmed on fresh boot.
[*][B]RIL race fix (rild.c)[/B] — rild now polls for /dev/radio/pttycmd1 (up to 15 s) before calling RIL_Init. Prevents null-funcs crash when rild starts before gsm0710muxd creates the ptty channels.
[*][B]Baseband version fix (GSMPhone.java)[/B] — added retry logic in EVENT_RADIO_ON: re-requests getBasebandVersion() and getIMEI() if the initial requests at radioState=0 got GENERIC_FAILURE from MTK RIL.
[*][B]zRAM enabled[/B] — ro.zram.default=25 activates ~120 MB compressed swap on boot via CM10 compcache service. Adjustable in Settings → Performance.
[*][B]Modem boot improved[/B] — modem now boots on first attempt (~7 s NORMAL_BOOT_ID vs previous 23 s WDT timeout/reset cycle).
[*][B]SIM PIN fix (IccCard.java)[/B] — MTK modem keeps radioState=UNAVAILABLE while a PIN-locked SIM waits for AT+CPIN, so EVENT_RADIO_ON never fires and the keyguard never showed the PIN prompt. Fixed by probing SIM status immediately in EVENT_RADIO_OFF_OR_NOT_AVAILABLE and retrying every 3 s until the RIL responds with PIN_REQUIRED. PIN dialog now appears correctly on boot.
[*]WiFi and Bluetooth confirmed working.
[*]Outgoing calls confirmed working; earpiece and microphone verified.
[*]Device tree cleanup: removed dead lgpservicestub source directory.
[/LIST]

[B]2026-06-22 — Build 1 (initial public test)[/B]
[LIST]
[*]First bootable CM10 build for LG-E450g / vee5ss.
[*]MediaTek boot image format via mtkbootimg (MTK KERNEL + ROOTFS headers).
[*]PowerVR SGX531 binary GPU blobs included.
[*]MTK CCCI radio stack: kernel modules + ccci_mdinit, ccci_fsd, ccci_rpcd, gsm0710muxd.
[*]Modem firmware (modem.img + DSP_ROM) included.
[*]Custom lights HAL (lights.mt6575.so) — fixes stuck notification LED bug in stock HAL.
[*]Sensor HAL: accelerometer, magnetometer, orientation, proximity via /dev/hwmsensor.
[*]External microSD via vold + storage_list.xml overlay.
[/LIST]

